### BullModule.forRootAsync

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/bull/blob/master/_autodocs/api-reference/bullmq-module.md

Static factory method to configure the BullMQ module asynchronously.

```APIDOC
## BullModule.forRootAsync

### Description
Registers a global BullMQ module with asynchronous shared configuration. Supports `useFactory`, `useClass`, `useExisting`, `inject`, `extraOptions`, `extraProviders`, and `imports`. The `extraOptions` is a top-level property of `SharedBullAsyncConfiguration`.

### Method
static

### Endpoint
`BullModule.forRootAsync(asyncBullConfig: SharedBullAsyncConfiguration): DynamicModule`
`BullModule.forRootAsync(configKey: string, asyncBullConfig: SharedBullAsyncConfiguration): DynamicModule`
`BullModule.forRootAsync(keyOrAsyncConfig: string | SharedBullAsyncConfiguration, asyncBullConfig?: SharedBullAsyncConfiguration): DynamicModule`

### Parameters
- `keyOrAsyncConfig` (string | SharedBullAsyncConfiguration) - Required - `configKey` or async-config object.
- `asyncBullConfig` (SharedBullAsyncConfiguration) - Required only when a `configKey` is given - supports `useFactory`/`useClass`/`useExisting`, `inject`, `extraOptions`, `extraProviders`, `imports`.

### Returns
A global `DynamicModule`. The `useFactory` for the shared config receives `inject: options.inject || []`; the `useClass`/`useExisting` path calls `optionsFactory.createSharedConfiguration()`.

### Usage Example
```ts
import { BullModule } from '@nestjs/bullmq';
import { ConfigService } from './config.service';

@Module({
  imports: [
    BullModule.forRootAsync({
      useFactory: (config: ConfigService) => ({
        connection: config.getRedisConnection(),
      }),
      inject: [ConfigService],
    }),
  ],
})
export class AppModule {}
```
```

