### registerQueueAsync

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/bull/blob/master/_autodocs/api-reference/bullmq-module.md

Registers BullMQ queues asynchronously in a NestJS module, allowing dynamic configuration of queue options via factories or classes.

```APIDOC
## registerQueueAsync

### Description
Registers BullMQ queues asynchronously in a NestJS module, allowing dynamic configuration of queue options via factories or classes.

### Method
registerQueueAsync

### Signature
```ts
static registerQueueAsync(...options: RegisterQueueAsyncOptions[]): DynamicModule;
```

### Parameters
- `options` (RegisterQueueAsyncOptions[]) - Required (variadic) - An array of options objects containing `name`, `configKey`, `imports`, `useFactory`/`useClass`/`useExisting`, `inject`, and `extraProviders`.

### Returns
- `DynamicModule` - A NestJS dynamic module that provides the queue providers.

### Usage Example
```ts
@Module({
  imports: [
    BullModule.registerQueueAsync({
      name: 'notifications',
      useFactory: () => ({ connection: { host: process.env.REDIS_HOST, port: 6379 } }),
    }),
  ],
})
export class NotificationsModule {}
```
```

