### BullModule.registerQueue

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/bull/blob/master/_autodocs/api-reference/bullmq-module.md

Static factory method to register queues and their processors.

```APIDOC
## BullModule.registerQueue

### Description
Registers a local BullMQ module with one or more queues. Each queue provider's factory creates the queue and its workers, and attaches an `onApplicationShutdown` hook to close workers, the queue, and optionally force-disconnect Redis.

### Method
static

### Endpoint
`BullModule.registerQueue(...options: RegisterQueueOptions[]): DynamicModule`

### Parameters
- `options` (RegisterQueueOptions[]) - Required (variadic) - `name`, `configKey`, `processors`, `connection`, `sharedConnection` (deprecated), `forceDisconnectOnShutdown` + any `QueueOptions` field.

### Returns
A local `DynamicModule` with option providers and queue providers. Each queue provider's factory calls `createQueueAndWorkers` which:
1. Creates the queue: `new queueClass(queueName, options)`.
2. For every `processors` entry creates a `workerClass` instance (concurrency etc. forwarded as worker options, plus `connection`, `sharedConnection`, `prefix` from the queue options).
3. Attaches `onApplicationShutdown`: closes all workers (`Promise.all(worker.close())`), closes the queue, and if `forceDisconnectOnShutdown` is truthy, force-disconnects Redis via `getConnectionStatus(this)` / `this.disconnect()` unless the status is already `'closed'`.

The module imports `coreModuleDefinition` as well.

### Usage Example
```ts
import { Module } from '@nestjs/common';
import { BullModule } from '@nestjs/bullmq';

@Module({
  imports: [
    BullModule.registerQueue({
      name: 'image-optimize',
      defaultJobOptions: { attempts: 2 },
      processors: [
        {
          name: 'resize',
          concurrency: 4,
          callback: async (job) => {
            await resizeImage(job.data);
          },
        },
      ],
    }),
  ],
})
export class ImageModule {}
```
```
